Day 35: Fix Your Eyes on Jesus | Tuesday of the Fifth Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
“Fix your eyes on Jesus.”
Not on the fear.
Not on the problem.
Not on the uncertainty.
On Him.

Welcome to Day 35 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection invites you to return your gaze to the One who sustains you. Endurance is not about pushing harder or pretending you’re strong — it grows when your focus shifts from what drains you to the One who walks with you through every valley.

This spoken‑word devotional reminds you that when your eyes drift to the storm, fear rises. When your eyes drift to yourself, doubt grows. But when your eyes return to Christ, faith steadies. He is the One who strengthens you, leads you, and holds you together when life feels heavy.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why endurance grows when your focus is on Christ

How Jesus steadies your heart in moments of worry or uncertainty

Why Lent teaches you to look beyond the struggle

A prayer to keep your eyes fixed on Jesus

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Jesus, keep my eyes on You.”

